{"title":"Career Roadmap: Instrumentation & Control Engineering → Instrumentation Engineer","role":"Instrumentation Engineer","summary":"An Instrumentation Engineer designs, installs, calibrates, maintains and improves systems that measure and control industrial processes.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Instrumentation & Control Engineering"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Domain","text":"Industrial Instrumentation, Process Control, Automation, PLC/SCADA & Industrial Systems"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Instrumentation Engineer designs, installs, calibrates, maintains and improves systems that measure and control industrial processes."},{"type":"p","text":"The role is especially important in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Oil & gas"},{"text":"Petrochemicals"},{"text":"Chemical plants"},{"text":"Power generation"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Food processing"},{"text":"Water treatment"},{"text":"Steel"},{"text":"Cement"},{"text":"Automotive"},{"text":"Renewable energy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical measurements include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Pressure"},{"text":"Flow"},{"text":"Level"},{"text":"pH"},{"text":"Vibration"},{"text":"Speed"},{"text":"Position"},{"text":"Density"},{"text":"Electrical parameters"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The core engineering loop is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Physical Process","Sensor","Transmitter","Signal Conditioning","PLC / DCS","Control Algorithm","Control Valve / Actuator","Physical Process","Feedback"]},{"type":"flow","items":["This makes the career a strong combination of electronics","control systems","automation","industrial processes."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Role Direction","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1–2"},{"text":"Engineering Student"},{"text":"Electric