easurement uncertainty"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Physical Quantity","Sensor","Transducer","Signal Conditioning","Measurement"]}]},{"heading":"Sensors & Transducers","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong knowledge of sensors for:"},{"type":"h","text":"Temperature"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RTD"},{"text":"Thermocouple"},{"text":"Thermistor"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Pressure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bourdon tube"},{"text":"Strain-gauge pressure sensors"},{"text":"Differential pressure transmitters"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Flow"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Orifice plate"},{"text":"Venturi"},{"text":"Rotameter"},{"text":"Magnetic flow meter"},{"text":"Coriolis flow meter"},{"text":"Ultrasonic flow meter"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Level"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Float"},{"text":"Differential pressure"},{"text":"Ultrasonic"},{"text":"Radar"},{"text":"Capacitive"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Proximity"},{"text":"Position"},{"text":"Speed"},{"text":"Vibration"},{"text":"Force"},{"text":"pH"},{"text":"Conductivity"}]}]},{"heading":"Signal Conditioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how raw sensor signals become usable control signals."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Amplification"},{"text":"Filtering"},{"text":"Isolation"},{"text":"Linearization"},{"text":"Noise reduction"},{"text":"Signal conversion"},{"text":"ADC"},{"text":"DAC"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important industrial signals include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"4–20 mA"},{"text":"0–10 V"},{"text":"Pulse/frequency signals"},{"text":"Digital communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sensor","Weak / Raw Signal","Signal Conditioning","4–20 mA / Digital Signal","PLC / DCS"]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Process Instrumentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how instrumentation is applied to real industrial processes."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Temperature measurement"},{"text":"Pressure measurement"},{"text":"Flow measurement"},{"text":"Level measurement"},{"text":"Analytical instrumentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand process variables:"},{"type":"h","text":"PV → Process Variable"},{"type":"h","text":"SP → Set Point"},{"type":"h","text":"MV → Manipulated Variable"},{"type":"h","text":"CV → Controlled Variable"}]},{"heading":"Control Systems","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Control engineering is a major part of the role."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Open-loop systems"},{"text":"Closed-loop systems"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Transfer functions"},{"text":"Block diagrams"},{"text":"Stability"},{"text":"Time response"},{"text":"Frequency response"},{"text":"Control-system modeling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Set Point","Controller","Actuator","Process","Sensor","Feedback"]},{"type":"p","text":"└──────────────→ Controller"}]},{"heading":"PID Control","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"PID is one of the most important practical control concepts."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"P — Proportional"},{"type":"h","text":"I — Integral"},{"type":"h","text":"D — Derivative"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PID tuning"},{"text":"Response characteristics"},{"text":"Overshoot"},{"text":"Settling time"},{"text":"Steady-state error"},{"text":"Stability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Temperature Set Point","PID","Control Valve","Heater / Process","Temperature Sensor","Feedback"]},{"type":"p","text":"Students should practice PID control through simulation before working with industrial equipment."}]},{"heading":"Year 2–3 — PLC Programming","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"PLC knowledge is highly valuable for industrial instrumentation roles."},{